        return primes[n - 1]

    # For larger n, use the Sieve of Eratosthenes to generate primes up to a limit.
    # Estimate upper bound: nth prime < n * (ln n + ln ln n) for n >= 6.
    # We'll increase limit until we have at least n primes.
